y correctly renders "drew 0 card(s)" (no pluralization suffix, count interpolated as-is) - confirmed via test, no change needed there. Same "owner never logged" gap also found in the Devil's orientAny (can reorient ANY player's piece, no ownership restriction - checkOrientAny/applyOrientAny): owner was computed for the newMinion-chaining decision but never pushed. Added `who` to the "orient" schema, new ORIENT.gnostica_target locale key; the plain "gnostica" key stays as both the ordinary-orient (always self, cmdOrient) AND Devil-self-target fallback, matching destroy's tile-case precedent for a result that never sets `who` at all. @done(26-08-22)
